{{!
    Airpay Section Header — Phase B0 iter 6 (2026-05-14)

    Small but used everywhere. Replaces ad-hoc <h3 class="airpay-dash__
    section-title"> + inline link pattern with a single partial that
    owns the spacing, typography, icon alignment, and optional
    "View all →" affordance.

    Always emits <h3> — most sections are section-level, and Mustache's
    lack of conditional template selection makes mixing h2/h3/h4 in one
    partial messier than helpful. For top-of-page <h2>, use a separate
    page-header partial.

    Context:
        title       (required) — header text (escaped)
        icon        (optional) — FA icon name without "fa-" prefix
        linkurl     (optional) — URL for "View all →" affordance
        linklabel   (optional) — overrides the default "View all"
        compact     (optional) — bool — drops bottom margin for tight
                                 stacked sections

    A11y:
      - <h3> is a real heading so screen reader users can navigate by
        section.
      - "View all" link has aria-label combining target + section name.

    Usage:
        {{> theme_airpayux/components/section_header }}
}}
<header class="airpay-section-header{{#compact}} airpay-section-header--compact{{/compact}}">
    <h3 class="airpay-section-header__title">
        {{#icon}}<i class="fa fa-{{icon}} airpay-section-header__icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{/icon}}
        <span>{{title}}</span>
    </h3>
    {{#linkurl}}
    <a class="airpay-section-header__link"
       href="{{linkurl}}"
       aria-label="{{#linklabel}}{{linklabel}}{{/linklabel}}{{^linklabel}}View all {{title}}{{/linklabel}}">
        {{#linklabel}}{{linklabel}}{{/linklabel}}{{^linklabel}}View all{{/linklabel}}
        <i class="fa fa-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </a>
    {{/linkurl}}
</header>
